/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Pick a small window fixed to the laboratory wall.
   - The molar flux NA is not the mass flux.
   - The mixture itself has a velocity.
   - Add and subtract cA u: NA = cA vA = cA u + cA(vA − u) = yA(NA + NB) + JA.
   - NA and NB are fixed-frame molar fluxes in mol/(m²·s); JA is the diffusion flux of A in mol/(m²·s); yA is the mole fraction of A.
   - Other frames have other names.
   - Molecular diffusion comes from random molecular motion.
   - The measured mean flux can contain both parts.
   - The molecular part uses DAB, the molecular diffusivity of the pair at that temperature and pressure.
*/
