/* book: lead: Fick's first law says a component diffuses down its concentration gradient, with flux proportional to the gradient. Fick's second law adds conservation of mass, so it predicts how concentration changes with time at a point. Together they turn a qualitative idea—ink spreading in water, oxygen entering a lung, dopant entering silicon—into equations an engineer can solve. This chapter states both law */
