/* book exam traps: Dropping the minus sign. If yA falls as z increases, JA is positive in the +z direction; a negative JA means flux is towards −z. | Using JA when the question asks for NA through a stagnant gas. Add the bulk term yA(NA + NB); the result contains the factor 1/(yB)_lm. | Treating D as constant for every fluid. Gas D changes little with composition, but liquid D can change strongly with concentration. | Assuming a straight-line profile always. It holds only at steady state with constant D and c, no reaction, no bulk flow and a flat path of constant area. | Flipping the reaction sign. A net production of A adds RA to the right side; a consumption term is negative. */
